Faxbot: the most compact fax coding a sent fax may use, measured on its own pages (spandsp 0.0.6; builder CA).

Before each attempt Faxbot measures the lossless codings MH, MR and MMR on
the fax's own pages (api/app/pages/coding.py) and, when the smallest one is
not what spandsp would take by itself, sets FAXBOT_COMPRESSION ("mh", "mr" or
"mmr") on the Originate (ami.py). After set_ecm, which offers Asterisk's own
set (MH, MR and MMR) at session start, SendFAX offers only the codings up to
the one named (faxbot_compressions in faxbot_t38_gateway.h, which the replay
proof compiles too): "mmr" offers MH, MR and MMR, "mr" offers MH and MR, "mh"
offers MH, which every fax machine takes. spandsp still takes the best coding
the receiving machine also has, and T.6 (MMR) only with error correction, so
the variable is a ceiling and never makes a machine get a coding it lacks.
Error correction is not changed. One NOTICE line per session names the
coding. Unset or anything else keeps Asterisk's own set; a received fax always
offers every coding.

--- a/res/res_fax_spandsp.c
+++ b/res/res_fax_spandsp.c
@@ -617,6 +617,38 @@
 #endif
 }
 
+/*!
+ * \brief Faxbot (0006): the most compact coding a sent fax may use, from FAXBOT_COMPRESSION ("mh", "mr" or "mmr").
+ *
+ * Faxbot measures MH, MR and MMR on the fax's own pages before dialing (api/app/pages/coding.py) and sets the
+ * smallest one this call may use; faxbot_compressions (faxbot_t38_gateway.h) turns it into the codings offered, a
+ * ceiling: spandsp still takes the best coding the receiving machine also has, and MMR only with error correction.
+ * Error correction is not changed here. Unset or anything else keeps Asterisk's own set (set_ecm); a received fax
+ * always offers every coding.
+ */
+static void faxbot_set_compressions(t30_state_t *t30_state, struct ast_fax_session *s)
+{
+	char coding[8] = "";
+	const char *value;
+	int supported;
+
+	if (!s->chan || !(s->details->caps & AST_FAX_TECH_SEND)) {
+		return;
+	}
+	ast_channel_lock(s->chan);
+	value = pbx_builtin_getvar_helper(s->chan, "FAXBOT_COMPRESSION");
+	if (value) {
+		ast_copy_string(coding, value, sizeof(coding));
+	}
+	ast_channel_unlock(s->chan);
+	supported = faxbot_compressions(coding);
+	if (!supported) {
+		return;
+	}
+	t30_set_supported_compressions(t30_state, supported);
+	ast_log(LOG_NOTICE, "Faxbot: %s offers codings up to %s\n", ast_channel_name(s->chan), coding);
+}
+
 static int spandsp_v21_new(struct spandsp_pvt *p)
 {
 	/* XXX Here we use MODEM_CONNECT_TONES_FAX_CED_OR_PREAMBLE even though
@@ -1196,6 +1228,8 @@
 	set_local_info(p->t30_state, s->details);
 	set_file(p->t30_state, s->details);
 	set_ecm(p->t30_state, s->details);
+	/* Faxbot (0006): the most compact coding measured for this fax's pages (FAXBOT_COMPRESSION). */
+	faxbot_set_compressions(p->t30_state, s);
 	t30_set_supported_modems(p->t30_state, spandsp_modems(s->details));
 
